{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7omwvnobzczpbexc46orstr3ori6wgyjn64fah7uvhbggmmhejiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. `c_src/` untouched; only `translation/` was modified.\n\n## One real bug found and fixed\n\n`c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA; c2Proxy pB;` — **uninitialised** C locals, i.e. a fixed pair of stack slots reused by every call from the same site. `c2MakeProxy` writes only `verts[0..count)`, so an unvalidated `c2GJKCache.iA/iB` index at or beyond `count` reads what an *earlier* call left there. The Rust used `c2Proxy::default()` (zeroed) per call.\n\nProven, not guessed: priming with AABB `{(100,200),(300,400)}` then reading indices 1/2/3 yields exactly `(5.76923, 3.84615)`, `(4.2, 5.6)`, `(1.47059, 5.88235)` — corners 1/2/3 of the *previous* AABB. I hand-derived all three through `c22`/`c2Witness` before writing any code. Fixed by modelling the proxies as thread-local persistent scratch (`ProxyScratch`), keyed by call depth so the boolean wrappers get their own slot. Locked in by `tests/phase_b_proxy_persistence.rs`, which I confirmed **fails** if per-call zeroing is reintroduced.\n\n## Scope limit worth your attention\n\nOne sub-case is unmatchable *by construction*, and I'd rather flag it than paper over it: when the index names a slot no preceding call wrote, C reads stack residue. In a harness that alternates `C.c2GJK`/`R.c2GJK` from one call site the frames overlap, so **the C's own answer changes** — `(5.769, 3.846)` alone vs `(0,0)` with a Rust call interleaved. The C isn't self-consistent there, so no implementation can be \"correct\". `difftest/diff` ships `NO_CACHE`/`CACHE_IDX0` knobs and comments that exact line accordingly; with either set it reports 0/21,300,002 failures. Evidence table and repro (`tools/probe_proxy_slot.c`) are in `ERRORS.md` → \"Scope\". The 752,063 residual failures in the unknobbed run are confined to this region.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Symbols:** 38 C / 38 Rust, diff empty both ways; 0 undefined non-libc.\n- **Phase B:** 70 `CONFIGS.md` rows, **Phase C:** 35 `ERRORS.md` rows — all checked, 84 tests, all comparisons bit-exact (`to_bits`, whole-struct byte compares), all via `libloading` on both `.so`s.\n- **All 4 configurations** green (debug/release × the only feature combo — crate declares no `[features]`).\n- Independent cross-check: `bits_test` 10M checks, `cache_test` 1.6M, `diff` 21.3M — 0 failures.\n- Stress run at `CAPSULE_N=40000` clean. No binary targets exist in either tree, so no stdout comparison applies.\n\n`translation/verify.sh` reproduces the whole thing end to end.\n\nTwo notes on the harness I built: NaN handling is bit-exact including payloads and signalling→quiet conversion, which is why the existing `*_ss` SSE helpers survived scrutiny. And I added `libloading` as a dev-dependency, which updated `Cargo.lock` with `cfg-if` and `windows-link`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2510,"cache_read_input_tokens":245555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2510,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ed8914d-6817-4736-8f37-e5881dd5b50c","uuid":"a41e416c-f700-4362-ab94-986fdcf3dd07","timestamp":"2026-09-05T07:07:56.368Z"}
